 4. 🎤 Barred reporters move to sidewalk 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Photos: Jose Luis Magana/AP, Doug Mills/The New York Times On the left: CNN senior White House reporter Betsy Klein, flashing an empty credential holder, reports across Pennsylvania Avenue from the White House complex yesterday. When she tried to enter, her badge was confiscated under President Trump's "ban" on CNN, MS NOW and Politico.

 On the right: Akayla Gardner, a White House correspondent for MS NOW, also delivered live hits from across the street after having her badge deactivated. All three organizations issued statements hinting at legal action. The New York Times , The Washington Post and AP released supportive statements. 

