 5. 🗞️ Deals eclipse lawsuits 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Axios research. Chart: Erin Davis/Axios Visuals Media deals with AI firms have dramatically outpaced lawsuits over the past two years, Kerry Flynn and Sara Fischer report in an Axios Media Trends Executive briefing. 

 Why it matters: The licensing market is developing faster than courts are establishing the underlying rules. Zoom in: News has moved furthest into the licensing market, although much of that momentum is coming from deals with smaller firms, like ProRata, rather than major companies like Anthropic. 

 Music and book companies have become more litigious over the past two years. Share this chart ... Subscribe to Axios Media Trends Executive . 

 
 
