 7. 🇨🇳 AI state dinner 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Photos: AFP via Getty Images Chinese President Xi Jinping arrives in D.C. this week for the first state visit by a Chinese leader in more than a decade: 

 AI will be a focus of the Trump-Xi summit at the White House on Thursday, and top tech moguls have scored invitations to the hot-ticket state dinner in the East Room.

 On the guest list, per Axios' Maria Curi and Courtenay Brown : David Sacks, Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang, Apple executive chair Tim Cook, OpenAI CEO Sam Altman, Goldman Sachs CEO David Solomon, Citi CEO Jane Fraser, Google and Alphabet CEO Sundar Pichai, plus Michael Dell, Jeff Bezos and Elon Musk. 🛬 When Xi's plane lands at Joint Base Andrews on Wednesday, Trump will be there to greet him. Trump typically meets foreign leaders at the White House.

 More on the visit . 
 
