 8. 🖼️ 1 for the road: L.A.&#x27;s new museum 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The new 300,000-square-foot Lucas Museum of Narrative Art in L.A.'s Exposition Park. Photo: Mario Tama/Getty Images "Star Wars" creator George Lucas called his Lucas Museum of Narrative Art a "temple to the people's art." Seventeen years after it was first envisioned, it'll open to the public on Tuesday in Los Angeles.

 The museum mixes popular and commercial art with fine art, drawn largely from the collections of Lucas and his wife and co-founder, businesswoman Mellody Hobson. What you'll see: 

 💫 The "Star Wars in Motion" exhibit shows vehicles used in the original trilogy and the Lucas-directed prequels. The outdoor paths feature statues of Carrie Fisher's Princess Leia, Natalie Portman's Padmé Amidala, Yoda and Grogu. 🎨 There are paintings by Norman Rockwell and Frida Kahlo and murals by Banksy and Diego Rivera. 🐶 "Poker Game," Cassius Marcellus Coolidge's kitschy 1894 painting of a group of dogs playing cards, hangs steps from a Kahlo self-portrait — a perfect merger of high and low art. Go deeper . 

 
 
